WEBVTT

01:01:27.882 --> 01:01:33.314
us collectively generating the conditions
whereby enough people get off their asses

01:01:33.338 --> 01:01:36.149
and start to tinker around and fix things.

01:01:36.173 --> 01:01:38.919
DB: Right. And I'm not sure
I've seen data on that.

01:01:38.943 --> 01:01:40.398
I've read philosophy about it.

01:01:40.422 --> 01:01:43.869
And so, if I wanted to motivate
people to do a cause, I would say,

01:01:43.893 --> 01:01:47.359
"If you join this, you can get
really close to people."

01:01:47.383 --> 01:01:49.635
Most of our thinking
is not for truth-finding.

01:01:49.659 --> 01:01:51.907
Most of our thinking
is for social bonding.

01:01:51.931 --> 01:01:54.014
We think the things will get us liked.

01:01:54.038 --> 01:01:57.808
And so, if -- I mean, global warming,

01:01:57.832 --> 01:02:00.584
you know, one of the opportunities
and one of burdens is,